{"id": "EUVD-2026-81882", "enisaUuid": "3fa995c7-8634-3125-bc1f-21cad05dca09", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Resize MST HDCP per-connector arrays to 32\n\nAMDGPU_DM_MAX_DISPLAY_INDEX is 31. It suggest a maximum number of\n32 connectors. But the way it's used is like MAX_DISPLAY_COUNT.\nHence we're off by one with DRM core, which supports a max of 32\nconnectors.\n\nRename AMDGPU_DM_MAX_DISPLAY_INDEX to AMDGPU_DM_MAX_DISPLAY_COUNT\nto match its actual use, and increase the size to 32 to match the\noriginally intended size.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:50:48", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/decea8279bec5a35413b2cb8e36951cca308fac0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac490fea9fe74f9d9975c5d8250c8719750589cd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/562d24ac214ba9530d88841088eb6adce5c537b5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0fa116a17b69a28712cdf209318e345b676d7f6c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/261e0fe4e2c99f687114b64b10b98db964b475f4"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90289", "GHSA-jm7v-p326-mf66"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2f549fb3-3d4c-32e8-ba3d-9b44c8156806", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82986fd631fa04bcedaefe11a6b3767601cbe84f <decea8279bec5a35413b2cb8e36951cca308fac0"}, {"id": "4165118e-ba96-36e2-806f-cfceae298f0d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "52965b78-c47d-3d8f-b8f4-8406c103c0b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "75358f1d-14bc-3fab-b6ea-a3848fbd4455", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.128 <5.16"}, {"id": "88b0f281-4f84-3295-a7a1-e3e73d0ad2f3", "product":